== (a) one-body symbol of the TOTAL energy current, E dE/dk, vs sawtooth k (NN-KG, m=1) ==
  k= 0.1: E dE/dk = sin k = +0.09983   sawtooth = +0.10000   mismatch = +0.00017
  k= 0.5: E dE/dk = sin k = +0.47943   sawtooth = +0.50000   mismatch = +0.02057
  k= 1.0: E dE/dk = sin k = +0.84147   sawtooth = +1.00000   mismatch = +0.15853
  k= 2.0: E dE/dk = sin k = +0.90930   sawtooth = +2.00000   mismatch = +1.09070
  k= 3.0: E dE/dk = sin k = +0.14112   sawtooth = +3.00000   mismatch = +2.85888
  -> with NN-KG matter the shift source P must have symbol sin k (= energy current); a sawtooth P
     leaves d/dt(scalar constraint) ~ div(J_E - P_saw) != 0 on the constraint surface.

